WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.654
Idea. Picture a pair of scales. Every transaction is recorded twice: once as a debit and once as a credit, for the same amount. So, on any date, all the debit balances should weigh exactly the same as all the credit balances.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:29.731
A trial balance is a list of every ledger balance on one date, in two columns: debit and credit. Here, bank and equipment are debits, capital is a credit, and both totals are five thousand dollars.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:39.307
To choose the column, remember: assets, expenses and drawings are debits. Liabilities, equity, income and provisions are credits.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:52.577
Method. Go down the list one account at a time. Decide its side, then copy the amount into that column without changing it. Add each column, and write both totals on the same line.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:01:10.311
Take extra care with the tricky items. A bank overdraft is a credit, because the business owes the bank. Provisions are credits. Returns inwards is a debit, but returns outwards is a credit. Receivables control is a debit, payables control a credit.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:21.917
If the totals differ and the question tells you to, add a suspense account on the smaller side. Here the credit side is four hundred short, so suspense goes in the credit column.

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:36.104
Worked example. Here is a real question from June 2024. Vaughn gives eighteen balances at 30 April 2024. We must prepare the trial balance. Eleven marks.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:50.613
Advertising is an expense, so debit. The bank loan is a liability, so credit. The bank overdraft is money owed to the bank, so credit too. Carriage inwards and drawings are debits. Equity is a credit.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:02:03.015
General expenses, opening inventory, machinery at cost and premises are debits. The provision for depreciation is a credit, and so is the mortgage, a long-term loan.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:17.239
Purchases, returns inwards and wages are debits. Revenue is a credit. Trade payables control is what Vaughn owes, a credit. Trade receivables control is what customers owe him, a debit.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:35.260
Now add each column. The eleven debits total four hundred and twenty-three thousand and eighty dollars. The seven credits total the same. They agree, so no suspense account is needed. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:47.406
Common mistake. A common mistake is putting the bank overdraft in the debit column, because bank is usually a debit. An overdraft is money owed, so it is a credit.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:56.062
Another is putting a provision on the debit side. Provisions for depreciation and for irrecoverable debts are always credits.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:08.917
Your turn. Now you try. Here are Lina's balances at 31 March 2026. Prepare her trial balance and check that the totals agree. Pause here and work it out.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:19.024
Answer. Drawings, equipment, purchases, trade receivables and wages are debits. Together they total sixty-three thousand dollars.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:30.094
The overdraft, capital, the provision, returns outwards and revenue are credits. They also total sixty-three thousand dollars, so the trial balance agrees.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:41.753
Remember: classify each balance, copy it into its column, add both columns, and use suspense only if the question tells you to. Now try the practice questions.
